# This repository is Windows-first, and `.github/scripts/*.sh` is executed by a
# Linux runner. A shell script committed with CRLF fails there on its shebang
# line -- `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` -- which names
# neither the file nor the line ending, so the error points nowhere near the
# mistake.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` already prevents this, but that is per-machine
# configuration and is not carried by a clone. This is.
*.sh text eol=lf
